> .arpis., On 12/07/2012 23:09:
>
>  The common way (speaking as a computer scientist) of avoiding variable
>> repetition (and variable naming issues) in formal methods is to use De
>> Bruijn indices (https://en.wikipedia.org/**wiki/De_Bruijn_index<https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/De_Bruijn_index>),
>> but this fails the requirement of fitting in human memory.
>>
>
